        "say": [
          "While OFI captures instantaneous queue adjustments, detecting toxic flow across longer horizons requires Volume-Synchronized Probability of Informed Trading (VPIN).",
          "VPIN measures the historical concentration of informed trading by slicing high-frequency market transaction data into constant-volume buckets of size $V$.",
          "Because calendar time suffers from severe intraday clustering (high volume at market open and close, low volume during lunch), volume-clock sampling normalizes information arrival rates.",
          "Within each volume bucket $\\tau$, trades are classified into buyer-initiated volume $V_\\tau^B$ and seller-initiated volume $V_\\tau^S$ using Bulk Volume Classification (BVC).",
          "The order imbalance for bucket $\\tau$ is the absolute difference $|V_\\tau^B - V_\\tau^S|$: in balanced, uninformed markets, buyer and seller volume are roughly equal.",
          "VPIN is computed as the rolling average of order imbalances across $N$ consecutive volume buckets divided by the total volume $N \\times V$.",
          "When informed participants trade aggressively in one direction, VPIN spikes towards 1.0, providing early warning of impending liquidity blackouts and flash crashes.",
          "Volume-synchronized probability of informed trading divides continuous market activity into constant volume buckets rather than arbitrary clock-time intervals. This volume clock transformation normalizes trading velocity and isolates toxic flow during aggressive institutional liquidation waves."
        ],
