          "The Add Order message ($A$) injects a new order reference ID, price level $P$, share count $Q$, and side (Bid or Ask) into the book.",
          "The Order Executed message ($E$) partially or completely fills a resting order, reducing its remaining queue quantity.",
          "The Order Cancel/Delete message ($D$ or $X$) removes unexecuted shares from the specified order ID, preserving queue priority for subsequent orders.",
          "The fundamental mathematical invariant of a valid continuous limit order book is the No-Cross Condition: $\\max(P_{\\text{bid}}) < \\min(P_{\\text{ask}})$.",
          "If the highest bid ever meets or exceeds the lowest ask, an instantaneous matching execution occurs, collapsing the crossed spread to zero.",
          "Mastering L3 book reconstruction is the foundational prerequisite for high-frequency market making and queue priority arbitrage strategies.",
          "Deterministic state maintenance guarantees that trading algorithms perceive the true microstructural state of exchange matching engines."
